WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.650
Begin with observations: color, clast size, roundness, sorting, bed thickness and

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.550
contacts. Red colors commonly reflect oxidation, while dark gray may accompany

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.790
organic material and low oxygen.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.870
These clues support interpretations when combined.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:21.110
Color alone does not uniquely identify land, water depth or one

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.170
depositional environment.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.250
Grading can record weakening flow or settling.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:29.010
Large cross beds in well-sorted sand support wind-built dunes.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:33.130
Mudcracks form when wet mud contracts during drying and may later

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.950
fill with sand. A mudcracked bed records exposure to drying, but

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.830
identifying the exact coastal or inland setting still needs context.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.350
Marine fossils support seawater deposition, while plant remains help interpret land

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.770
and climate context. In the supplied examples, cross beds slope down-current,

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.410
while imbricated river clasts lean against the current.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.370
Asymmetric ripples can record one flow direction;

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.010
symmetric ripples commonly reflect back-and-forth waves.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.810
Keep the indicators and their directions distinct.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:08.890
The example begins with well-sorted, cross-bedded dune sandstone, then shell-bearing beach

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.290
sand, then marine shale and reef limestone.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.990
This upward passage records a transgression.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.350
Younger sand with land plants and coal records a later retreat

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:21.150
of the sea. The interpretation follows the changing evidence at one

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:21.570
location.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.970
Angular granite boulders in muddy breccia cap that example.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.610
Limited rounding and nearby granite terrain support debris flows from steep

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.290
mountains. This is a later tectonic and sediment-supply episode.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:38.670
Preserve the distinction between the observed fragments and the inferred setting,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.610
and do not transfer this five-unit example onto the separate four-unit

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:43.450
plateau investigation.
